# Tinybones' "you may cast" is a choice made as the ability resolves (CR 608.2g). Bot2's Llanowar Elves are in its graveyard
# (it bolted them). On turn 3 Bot1 attacks and declines: the Elves stay in Bot2's graveyard. On turn 5 Bot1 has tapped its
# Mox Jet for Dark Ritual first, so it has nothing to pay with: it accepts, cannot pay and gives the cast up (CR 733.1),
# and the Elves stay again. (The sibling scenario, tinybones-casts-a-creature-card-..., is the positive control.)

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Tinybones, the Pickpocket
Dark Ritual
Plains x18

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Emerald
Llanowar Elves
Lightning Bolt
Island x16

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Tinybones, the Pickpocket.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Tinybones, the Pickpocket)
Bot1.Decline
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Dark Ritual.Cast
Bot1.Attack(Tinybones, the Pickpocket)
Bot1.Accept
Bot1.Cancel
[T5 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Turn = 5
Bot2.Life = 18
Bot2.Graveyard = Llanowar Elves; Lightning Bolt
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Jet; Tinybones, the Pickpocket
